------------------------------------------------------------------------
Music theory material — credits
------------------------------------------------------------------------

The harmony feature classifies music into the 7 families and 33 "Scales of
Harmonies" described by Oliver Prehn (NewJazz) in his lesson "ALL ABOUT MUSICAL
SCALES - A COMPLETE GUIDE!!!" (https://youtu.be/Vq2xt2D3e3E) and its overview
sheet "The Scales of Harmonies". The family numbering, the rules that yield the
33 scales, the "systematic names" and the five-column layout shown in the app
are his work. Support him: https://www.patreon.com/newjazz - https://www.newjazz.dk

The app also bundles a colour-coded study sheet (assets/docs/scales-of-harmonies-*.pdf,
source docs/scales/) that reproduces the data of his overview table - families, names,
interval steps, systematic names, chords - with his credit and support links. Its
introduction and footnote are paraphrased, not copied; the layout and the blue/red
whole-tone colour code are by Steve Nodock.

No licence is stated for that material (checked on newjazz.dk, 2026-09-19), so
it is NOT covered by this project's Apache-2.0 licence and all rights remain
with its author. Scale names and interval patterns are common music theory;
the detection code is original work of this project. DuoMix Fader is not
affiliated with or endorsed by Oliver Prehn.

